ries it would pack. With --json, one\n  metais.pack/1 document.\n\nRefusals:\n  limit.invalid\n      A --limit names no limit, gives a malformed value, or tries to raise one.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  limit.package\n      The package, or the package's bytes as pack writes them, breach one of its\n      limits; nothing was written.\n      Next: metais limits\n  output.destination.in_package\n      The package file would be inside one of the layout trees of the source\n      directory, or be its manifest.\n      Next: metais pack <dir> --out <path>\n  output.destination.not_directory\n      A directory above the package file exists and is not a directory.\n      Next: metais pack <dir> --out <path>\n  output.destination.nothing_written\n      The package file could not be written, and nothing was: its directory does\n      not exist, what stands at its name is not a regular file, a temporary file\n      .metais-tmp-<h> is left beside it, or a write failed.\n      Next: metais pack <dir>\n  package.container.second_end_record\n      An entry of the package pack built puts the end of central directory\n      signature in the package's final 65,557 bytes, so a reader refuses the\n      package; nothing was written.\n      Next: metais pack <dir>\n  usage.archive_to_terminal\n      --out - is given, and standard output is a terminal.\n      Next: metais pack <dir> --out <path>\n  usage.bad_value\n      A flag's value is missing, or is not one the flag accepts, or a flag that\n      takes no value is given one.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  usage.bad_value\n      --out is empty, or names a file whose name metais will not write.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  usage.not_a_source_directory\n      The operand is a packed package, which pack does not read: it packs a\n      source directory.\n      Next: metais unpack <package> --to <dir>\n  usage.package_from_stdin\n      The package operand is -, standard input.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  usage.repeated_flag\n      A flag that may be given once is given again.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  usage.unexpected_operand\n      An operand the command does not take.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n  usage.unknown_flag\n      An argument that is not a flag the command accepts, an abbreviated flag,\n      or one-letter aliases written together.\n      Next: metais pack --help\n\n  Each line below is a family of codes: how many there are, the cause they share\n  and their next step. 'metais help refusals pack' lists every code, and help\n  --json gives each code's own cause.\n\n  collection.* (5)          An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  csv.* (7)                 An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  example.* (9)             An example fails. Next: metais test <dir>\n  example.layout (1)        An example's layout (layout), an error.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  input.* (52)              An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  json.* (5)                An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  limit.exceeded (1)        An example's inputs are refused (exceeded).\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  limit.exceeded.* (2)      An example's output is refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  manifest.* (44)           The manifest breaks one of its rules.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  manifest.guide_link_missing (1)\n                            The manifest (guide link missing), a warning.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  manifest.input.* (2)      The manifest, an error. Next: metais check <dir>\n  markdown.* (3)            An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  output.* (35)             An example's output fails its validation.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  output.container.* (3)    A container's profile, an error.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  output.container.space (1)\n                            A container's profile (container: space), a warning.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  output.* (2)              An example's output is refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n  output.declaration.validate_kind (1)\n                            An output's declaration (declaration: validate\n                            kind), an error. Next: metais check <dir>\n  output.path.* (8)         An output's literal path, an error.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  package.* (47)            The package is refused. Next: metais check <dir>\n  package.layout.* (2)      The package's tree, a warning.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  report.step_skipped (1)   The report (step skipped), an info.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  schema.* (10)             An input schema is refused. Next: metais check <dir>\n  schema.* (3)              A schema, an error. Next: metais check <dir>\n  schema.* (2)              A schema, a warning. Next: metais check <dir>\n  template.* (15)           A template is refused. Next: metais test <dir>\n  template.* (6)            A template or a manifest expression, a warning.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  template.* (9)            An output's path, when or for_each does not parse.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  template.* (8)            A template does not parse, an error.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  template.* (11)           A template or a manifest expression, an error.\n                            Next: metais check <dir>\n  yaml.* (13)               An example's inputs are refused.\n                            Next: metais test <dir>\n\nExamples:\n  metais pack\n      Checks, tests and packs the source directory in the working directory into\n      <name>-<version>.metais there.\n  metais pack report --out dist\n      Packs the source directory report into dist/<name>-<version>.metais, dist\n      being an existing directory.\n  metais pack --out -\n      Writes the package to standard output, which must be a file or a pipe, not\n      a terminal.\n  metais pack --dry-run --json\n      Checks, tests and builds the package, writes nothing, and prints its size\n      and digest as one metais.pack/1 document.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TTzkbZFiaU8Xv6nBo18wDi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
