{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFXZKbDk7RR3RgciHSzj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added an optional `due` date to the invoice package and repacked `invoice.metais` in place. `metais check` and `metais test` pass, and a test invoice with a due date renders it.\n\nI made the field optional, not required, so existing billing jobs keep validating without changes. The example inputs and their expected HTML are unchanged. Say if you want it required.\n\nChanges, all in the package source:\n- **`inputs/invoice.schema.json`**: a new `due` property, a `date`-format string, placed after `issued`. It rejects values that aren't dates.\n- **`templates/invoice.html.liquid`**: when `due` is given, the page prints `<p class=\"invoice-due\">Due …</p>` below the issued line. When it's left out, nothing is printed.\n- **`metais.yaml`**: the guide now mentions the due date.\n\nI left the package `version` at 1.0.0. An optional field is a backwards-compatible addition, so 1.1.0 would be the usual bump if you want consumers to see the change.\n\nThe original is saved at `scratch/ux-haiku2/backup/invoice.metais.orig`. The editable source is in `scratch/ux-haiku2/invoice-src`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":50376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a2a5d9a-b8c2-45fc-b4be-89bb204fae8a","uuid":"feff5fd8-2a58-460d-bc87-0a806585e563","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:18:56.848Z","request_id":"req_011CgFXZK4iyX9d4a1mzfN1B"}
